#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643195b8-5f3c-5dec-a199-1d4e1566d7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636844} {:answer/id #uuid "ab69d199-b8fe-570c-872d-ce2b5bd7a3b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636969} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe6b9bb-289d-560f-a1f6-fa661bc9a8a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636999} {:answer/id #uuid "db4125cf-daf8-57ba-ab40-6725dd625804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637051} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6a29d3-f315-52df-9f3d-fdc297bf21be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637116} :answer-field/id #uuid "f566f2c2-8864-5e73-a36e-4bddc02ba233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b137dad-7db4-50cb-b5c8-f93f31b8129d" :question/math-academy-id "q-18253" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1-2p & 4 & 2p+1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nis $-126,$  find the value of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1-2p & 4 & 2p+1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =(1-2p)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-4\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(2p+1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-2p)\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 2+(2p+1)\\cdot (-20) \\\\  & =6-12p-8-40p-20 \\\\  & =-52p-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-126,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-52p-22 & =-126 \\\\ -52p & =-104 \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639182 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33ba08da-9f5a-52d8-9bd9-567d6804bb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-{e}^{u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638718} {:answer/id #uuid "59f12bcd-4bf5-5853-b09a-118edf45b7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4u}+{e}^{3u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638785} {:answer/id #uuid "6531df97-a0f5-53cd-a7f1-b6ea5924c70e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638801} {:answer/id #uuid "75783e54-1171-5d5c-8402-cb1482ba7623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{2u}-{e}^{3u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638831} {:answer/id #uuid "be89115a-ad65-5b7a-bdc4-2ebd69a522c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{e}^{3u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638964}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186638831} :answer-field/id #uuid "42adc3cd-b96d-5012-8e9d-3fc32c49bc59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2f68c183-5310-55e6-bbe3-419bef3f8dfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-161791" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=v{e}^{2u},\\,y={e}^{u}+w,\\,z=2u+w.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2v{e}^{2u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={e}^{2u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & ={e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2v{e}^{2u} & {e}^{2u} & 0 \\\\ {e}^{u} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2v{e}^{2u} & {e}^{2u} \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2v{e}^{2u} & {e}^{2u} \\\\ {e}^{u} & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0-2{e}^{2u})+(0-{e}^{u+2u}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2u}-{e}^{3u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d42376-2a67-5205-bc31-6029158d622c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4x^{2}}{121}+\\frac{y^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640346}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640346} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebba8b17-515a-5650-ae77-45e9d1280e10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3105dab3-bbf2-5f61-bf47-d3d107d36609" :question/math-academy-id "q-277920" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6b511e6494fc9f5ec653321f29ae2628c48222ef42f591f4ce39a36c60948481.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{11}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{121}{4}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f7ec6d-e409-500e-ac06-44968617b98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643297} {:answer/id #uuid "3aaa549a-4c70-5f6d-96ed-2b88fcd9a5df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643306} {:answer/id #uuid "56f3b578-6c76-5bbb-8f8d-0b7ac0b32290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643309} {:answer/id #uuid "582fb0d7-708d-5d51-92df-507131f40950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643310} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba8f99a-c6be-541f-baa6-8d99641b194e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643315}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643315} :answer-field/id #uuid "34100d4e-936d-50ec-9c50-3f50c79f6ddf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "10aa925b-dbc8-583e-a476-be7dc1ebb577" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bddd8b3ba7352cd58667179d8b01c9c7f0ef523e4646e7c459ab577023356b64.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=6$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b043f4d-a341-5b61-855b-76770e803196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643314} {:answer/id #uuid "af9e7843-2bac-5513-b4d2-7dd7e1a0fa52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643318} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9ba515-fc97-5551-97ec-93537721f718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643323} {:answer/id #uuid "e129dd58-a0db-5850-bc30-232d21c53170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643324} {:answer/id #uuid "f62e89d2-63ef-5980-8e1d-895b89e30ebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643314} :answer-field/id #uuid "38b3db48-afa1-58f0-a70f-9bbf2c4a9dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2d5b8136-3aa3-595e-a435-3170a438f38d" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bbf58f80060415a5f773150d354f0548fbb37f9617929e4f86929e78ef1c572.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da5abfd-b2f1-56a5-91e8-9ec150222b01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643307} :answer-field/id #uuid "b339082a-5e0a-5e99-9892-39a183fff595" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "81a18912-3a04-554c-8ece-d62e8b2acca3" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4eb7e5fed25a147865a356a491c551d745f58730ad9c3fe4c333c6f2e0d1cfca.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=9$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{9}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22519a3e-bc57-5bda-a294-ac35c6688b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643300} {:answer/id #uuid "50a9aa28-fa7c-511d-8f1c-55d32b0d4759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643308} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbd8042-8e84-58c5-a611-494b5e0993ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643316} {:answer/id #uuid "adef1e59-bc2d-59e8-bc21-2a03211c611a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643317} {:answer/id #uuid "c94d68f8-0050-5bc4-84ac-fb20e489e238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643322}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643308} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6accd27-cec0-5c97-9aa7-ae9918860741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "931bbd9e-c39f-5a0a-8955-62b5e5e67af7" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9c992df95e92ddb3897feb6503bcde61cc7b38866584ca0153451928ec6a00a8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=9$ and the vertical radius has length $b=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{9}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f41b8a5-f46b-5d11-b1aa-4c05b08748c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643299} {:answer/id #uuid "36f0c1db-09a2-5ed5-9707-0d8c5012a4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643304} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5b2dd7-2578-5284-97f5-0a576c1cb3bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643311} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f6f32c-81c3-5fba-87c8-d64fd75f8941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643320} {:answer/id #uuid "c884b95e-8a42-582e-831a-9d4624c47d80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643304} :answer-field/id #uuid "2383c712-d996-5f49-bc9e-5970f28d4fe4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e63f0242-ac59-5a55-acfe-ce9b86f7de17" :question/problem "![](images/fd/fd5fe8314e19850aaa2650cc0cc05b1ba959f20679b4406ce2e8d3fe4985af0f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=6$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88936164-ad75-5c2a-ac39-447783eb30ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643338} :answer-field/id #uuid "f225dbcc-107a-5cad-b37c-67e3e5250406" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "76432b8a-6e98-5e8b-b9d7-ed568c39aa85" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d96b8c0c94500417798e1d80d51ae4a1dfddc6999c77f5ae693700e964c0d362.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19cc39cc-d40d-5a32-8319-4dd9398748fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643331} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7dd2b3-5543-591c-90bd-058b073767ca" :answer/t